# NOTE: Git LFS is intentionally NOT used for the data/models/ asset set.
#
# GitHub Pages (this site is served from the repo via "deploy from a branch")
# does NOT resolve Git LFS objects -- it serves the ~130-byte LFS POINTER text
# instead of the real binary, which breaks the .glb/.png loaders. GitHub Pages
# also caps a published site at 1 GB.
#
# So the published asset set is kept small (geometry GLBs + 512px perf PNG
# textures + hero thumbnails, ~230 MB) and committed as PLAIN git blobs that
# Pages serves correctly. The high-quality .dds set and the multi-angle shots/
# gallery are NOT committed (gitignored); they are regenerated locally by
# scripts/convert_msh.py and can be moved to an external host later.
